# pdxsock -- caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none.
#
# pdxsock's role: netcat-adjacent general TCP/UDP client + server
# (paideia-os design/networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md §7). TCP
# client, TCP server, TCP mirror-echo server, and (as of v1.3.0,
# pdxsock#6) connected-UDP client are all wired to the R72.M1-005 /
# R100-PREP-002 (sysnos 87..94, extended to SOCK_DGRAM) socket syscall
# family. UDP server (a bound-not-connected `-l -u` listener) remains
# out of scope per §7.2 -- it would need sys_recvfrom's peer-address
# out-params (SC+ 97) threaded into the generic `-l` path, which this
# tool does not do (the mirror server sidesteps the need by fixing the
# peer via sys_connect instead of discovering it via recvfrom).
#
# Kind rationale:
#   KIND_USER          -- invoker attribution (audit record identity);
#                         every satellite in the R100 wave lists this.
#   KIND_TCP_SOCKET    -- mandatory here because the TCP client path
#                         (socket + connect + send + recv + shutdown),
#                         the TCP server path (socket + bind + listen +
#                         accept + recv + send + shutdown), and the TCP
#                         mirror-server path (same setup as the server,
#                         recv+send in the reverse-direction pump) all
#                         fault without cap-slot 0 holding a TCP socket
#                         cap once sys_socket returns. The parent
#                         process (init / shell / a launcher) must have
#                         SEND (0x2) + RECV (0x1) + INVOKE (0x8)
#                         available or the first sys_send / sys_recv
#                         refuses with -EACCES.
#   KIND_UDP_SOCKET    -- optional. As of v1.3.0 (pdxsock#6) the `-u
#                         <host> <port>` client path is REAL (connected-
#                         UDP: socket + connect + send + recv +
#                         shutdown over the same sysnos as TCP, per
#                         R100-PREP-002). Stays optional because `-u`
#                         is an opt-in invocation shape, not every
#                         pdxsock run touches a UDP socket -- a parent
#                         that never grants this cap still gets a full
#                         TCP client/server/mirror.
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT  -- optional; documentation-only at v1.1-B.
#                         The v1.1-B semantic-pipe emission wire
#                         (paideia-os/pdxsock #16) uses
#                         `sys_semantic_send` (SC+ ID 115), which
#                         takes NO cap slot -- schema is opaque to
#                         the kernel and the producer is
#                         capability-ungated at R107-M0-001. The
#                         entry is retained so a future
#                         KIND_SEMANTIC_PIPE recv-side cap (arriving
#                         with the consumer wave) has a stable spot
#                         to land without a caps.decl churn.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit)
!KIND_TCP_SOCKET         0x00B   # READ (0x1) + SEND (0x2) + INVOKE (0x8)
 KIND_UDP_SOCKET         0x00B   # optional -- real connected-UDP client since v1.3.0 (M3-001)
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # optional -- documentation-only (see above)
